Body:
It looks like you are using MiMo v2.5 Free from OpenCode Zen. This happens because the metadata for MiMo v2.5 Free is incorrectly configured in [models.dev](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/blob/f1a9be19f62c24474d27947d5236067504dd755a/providers/opencode/models/mimo-v2.5-free.toml#L26) (where OpenCode fetches its default model list):

```toml
[modalities]
input = ["text", "image", "audio", "video"]
output = ["text"]
```

You can manually add pdf input to your OpenCode configuration to override the default settings:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "opencode": {
      "models": {
        "mimo-v2.5-free": {
          "modalities": {
            "input": ["audio", "video", "text", "image", "pdf"]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> BTW, interestingly enough, when using MiMo v2.5 via the official Xiaomi MiMo API, PDF input cannot be enabled this way—even though MiMo v2.5 is advertised as an alternative to the omni-modal MiMo v2 Omni, which is explicitly listed as supporting PDF input on [models.dev](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/blob/f1a9be19f62c24474d27947d5236067504dd755a/providers/xiaomi/models/mimo-v2-omni.toml#L30). Does anyone happen to know why?
